# Rules: Sectoral Trade Climate Code

- Input-output tables, SAMs and CGE benchmarks must balance, and the balance check is automated in tests
- A CGE or trade model must reproduce its benchmark data before any scenario is run
- State closure rules, the numeraire and the trade-balance treatment; report results under at least two closures where they matter
- Elasticities and damage-function parameters are sourced; scenario results include a sensitivity range
- Document sector and region classifications and all concordances between data sources
- Emissions accounting conventions (scope, gases, production vs. consumption basis) are stated with results
